Think: For each path in file_paths.txt, run stat to get size in bytes and write lines "size<TAB>path" to sizes_raw.txt, using awk to safely handle paths and fall back to 0 on errors.

Act: bash

```bash
awk '{
  path=$0;
  gsub(/"/, "\\\"", path);
  cmd = "stat -c \"%s\t%n\" \"" path "\" 2>/dev/null";
  cmd | getline out;
  close(cmd);
  if(out == "") { out = "0\t" $0 }
  print out
}' /home/user/experiment/.size_calc/file_paths.txt > /home/user/experiment/.size_calc/sizes_raw.txt
